# ── Public site URL (used for canonical URLs, sitemap, OG tags) ──
# No trailing slash. Set to your real domain in production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://ozzo.co.in

# ── Supabase (wacrm project) — used server-side to store inquiries ──
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://gxurqwpfvfktmreqmzqb.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# ── Email alerts for new inquiries (optional but recommended) ──
# Uses Resend (https://resend.com). Leave RESEND_API_KEY empty to disable
# email — inquiries are still saved to the database.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# Where new-lead alerts are sent (your sales/team inbox):
INQUIRY_NOTIFY_EMAIL=hello@ozzo.co.in
# Verified "from" address on your Resend domain:
INQUIRY_FROM_EMAIL=OZZO Website <notifications@ozzo.co.in>

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# WhatsApp lead alerts (optional)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# When a visitor submits the inquiry form, the lead is ALWAYS saved to
# Supabase and emailed via Resend. These variables add a third delivery:
# a WhatsApp message to the team, sent by the server with no action
# needed from the visitor.
#
# Leave them all unset and nothing breaks — the alert is skipped exactly
# the way the Resend alert is skipped without a key.
#
# Pick ONE transport.
#
# Transport A — any BSP, automation tool, or OZZO's own CRM.
# Receives POST {to, text, lead} as JSON. Checked first when set.
# WHATSAPP_ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=
# WHATSAPP_ALERT_WEBHOOK_SECRET=   # optional; sent as "Authorization: Bearer ..."
#
# Transport B — Meta WhatsApp Cloud API directly.
# The SENDER must be a number registered to the Cloud API. That number
# cannot also be signed in to consumer WhatsApp, so it has to be a
# different number from the one printed on the site — which is the
# RECIPIENT below, and can stay on a normal phone.
# WHATSAPP_ALERT_TOKEN=            # permanent System User access token
# WHATSAPP_ALERT_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=  # the sender's Phone Number ID from Meta
#
# Shared by both. Digits only, country code first, no + or spaces.
# Defaults to contact.whatsappNumber in src/lib/site.ts.
# WHATSAPP_ALERT_TO=919227126301
#
# Cloud API only. A business-initiated message needs an APPROVED template;
# without one WhatsApp only delivers inside a 24h window the recipient
# opened, so set this before relying on the alert. Category: UTILITY.
# Body must contain exactly six placeholders, in this order:
#   {{1}} name  {{2}} phone  {{3}} company  {{4}} team size  {{5}} page  {{6}} message
# WHATSAPP_ALERT_TEMPLATE=website_lead_alert
# WHATSAPP_ALERT_TEMPLATE_LANG=en
